{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact clean head 1d3081c4b7c885e7a13911e5cee3239d1722627a on request/whoami-attendance-current-main-integration.\n\nEvery gate and probe below ran with `git rev-parse HEAD` in the same command, and the head was re-read afterwards. It never moved. I reviewed in my own detached scratch worktree at that commit, not the implementer's checkout, and removed it afterwards. I did not edit, merge, ratify, push, or touch any remote.\n\nSTRUCTURE. The commit is a two-parent merge with exactly the stated parents: 41c9fc062cd2cb785d372c9cec4ef694da1dba52 (railway main) and 91b2cae54c6beabc1c83f6567de21f4c1a018e5b (reviewed whoami). Current main is 41c9fc06, so main is an ancestor by construction. The scratch checkout was clean at the exact head before and after every run, and `git diff --check` was clean. The merge is the only commit the branch adds over either parent, and it carries `Rests-On: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6d5e5709797c1a1d41dce64a80a259082e25e02e`, the integration request. Every commit on the source side back to the merge base also carries a Rests-On trailer.\n\nRECONCILIATION. I compared the merged tree against both parents rather than trusting the merge message.\n\nAgainst parent 41c9fc06 the only changes are the whoami work: cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go and main_test.go, internal/app/app.go and app_test.go, internal/service/server.go and server_test.go, internal/statusview/actor.go and view_test.go, docs/reference.md. Nothing under ui/ or internal/service/uidist/ differs at all, so the railway UI source and the committed browser embed survive byte-for-byte from main.\n\nAgainst parent 91b2cae the only changes are the railway: ui/src, ui/test, ui/package.json, ui/package-lock.json, and the generated uidist. No file under cmd/, internal/app, internal/service/server.go, internal/statusview, or docs/ differs, so the reviewed whoami behaviour and its documentation survive byte-for-byte from the approved source head.\n\nThe two contributions are therefore disjoint apart from the generated embed, which is where the conflict was. I checked the resolution is a real rebuild rather than a preference for one side. Parent 91b2cae changed no ui/ source at all; its bundle change over the merge base was a catch-up of an embed that had drifted behind already-committed base source (the added tokens are \"retired\" and \"label\", which base ui/src already used). Main's bundle contains that same catch-up plus the railway. I then rebuilt from the merged source with `make ui-check`: vite reproduced index-D9L7B-wU.js and index--ynpQeC8.css byte-identically to the committed files, and `git status --porcelain -- internal/service/uidist` was empty afterwards. The committed embed is exactly what the combined source builds to, so nothing from either side was silently dropped. `npm ci \u0026\u0026 npm test` in ui/ passed.\n\nMUTATIONS. I re-ran all eight semantic mutations myself in the scratch worktree, one at a time, restoring to a clean exact head between each. Each one produced a real behavioural failure.\n\n1. Removing the `ProjectionVersion` equality check in currentResidentOrientation: TestWhoamiRejectsUntrustedOrUnboundedResidentAnswers/projection_version_mismatch fails, the forged answer is returned with degraded false.\n2. Removing `orientation.Frontier.Depth \u003c 0`: .../negative_depth fails, Depth:-1 is returned with degraded false.\n3. Removing the required `You.Name` / `You.Kind` / `You.MembershipEvent`: .../missing_name, .../missing_kind and .../missing_member all fail.\n4. Removing `w.snapshotSource = SnapshotSourceIncrementalTail` from acceptSnapshot: internal/app TestSnapshotCachesTheVerifiedHead fails, reporting the accepted local append as \"verified_signed_checkpoint_tail\".\n5. `orientationTimeout` 2s to 10s. I first relaxed the literal assertion in the test to `10*time.Second` so the tautology could not fire. The test still failed, and failed on behaviour: \"stalled resident was not bounded: elapsed=10.312545417s\".\n6. `orientationResponseLimit` 64\u003c\u003c10 to 1\u003c\u003c20. Again I relaxed the literal assertion in the test to `1\u003c\u003c20` first. The test still failed, and failed on behaviour: the .../oversized subtest accepted a payload the real bound rejects.\n7. Making whoami take the ordinary attend path instead of attach: TestWhoamiDoesNotAttendBeforeOrdinaryTool fails, and the package then hangs until the 5-minute test timeout on the stalled-resident case, which is direct evidence for the comment's claim that the presence announce is a live side effect outside the two-second bound.\n8. Reducing the retry loop from two attempts to one: TestWhoamiRetriesOneConcurrentFrontierMove fails with calls=1 and a degraded fallback where a coherent resident answer was available.\n\nBoth of the literal-only assertions (5 and 6) are therefore load-bearing at this head, not merely self-confirming. That was worth re-proving here rather than inheriting: the assertions themselves are unchanged from the source head, but the constants they guard sit in a file this merge did not touch, and a merge is exactly where such a pairing can silently come apart.\n\nGATES. On the exact head, before mutations: vet, build, test, race all exit 0, plus ui npm test and make ui-check. After restoring from the last mutation I re-ran the whole set on the restored tree, again pinned to the head, and vet, test, race and build all exit 0 with a clean `git status --porcelain` and clean `git diff --check` before and after.\n\nSTANDING LIMIT, RE-WEIGHED AND STILL NOT BLOCKING. whoami prefers the loopback resident's answer, and currentResidentOrientation binds that answer to local durable evidence only on genesis, exact head read before and after, fingerprint, projection version, and shape bounds. The content of name, kind, membership event and the role set beyond the presence of \"participant\" is not compared against the local projection. A rogue local process holding 127.0.0.1:7777 can therefore make whoami report a fabricated identity with degraded false.\n\nI re-derived this from the code at this head rather than carrying the earlier finding forward, and I re-weighed it. It does not block, for three reasons. The attacker must already be a local process on the user's machine, and cannot forge signatures, so no durable act can be produced; the damage is confined to what orientation displays, and a misled agent's attempt to use a role it does not hold is judged ineffective by the fold and stays visible. The omission is also a deliberate trade: the fast path deliberately avoids local replay, which is what makes warm orientation sub-second at signed depth, and a full content cross-check would reintroduce exactly that cost. Most importantly, this head adds zero delta here: cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go is byte-identical to the previously reviewed and approved 91b2cae, so the integration does not change how much whoami trusts the resident in either direction.\n\nIt also already has durable follow-up work assigned rather than being an open question: request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5c4df469312e80f3d61467c2b7acd3fbd9524e7e, \"Settle what whoami owes a reader about resident-supplied identity\", is open and names the two honest outcomes. That request is the right place to close this, not this review.\n\nThe artifact statement's own claims all check out: exact parents, conflicts confined to generated uidist, resolution by combined-source rebuild, final UI and embed tree equal to railway main, whoami and backend and docs tree equal to 91b2cae.\n\nNOT VERIFIED. I did not review the railway UI feature itself or the whoami design on their merits; both arrived already approved on their own heads and this review is scoped to whether the integration preserves them. I did not run the spike target. I checked the bundle's byte identity to main and its reproducibility from the merged source, but I did not read the minified output for semantic equivalence beyond the deterministic rebuild, which I consider the stronger evidence anyway.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0718b5043cc3772630de2758de8d0c3a8dea3999","head":"1d3081c4b7c885e7a13911e5cee3239d1722627a","verdict":"approved"}}